$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=abelid  LOC_AFTER=?

* Abel summation (partial summation) for a Dirichlet-series partial sum: the sum of ` ( ( A ` k ) x. ( k ^c -u Z ) ) ` over ` ( 1 ... N ) ` is the boundary term plus the sum of the partial sums against the differences of ` ( k ^c -u Z ) `.  This is ` abel_identity ` of Route Z's LGrowth.lean, from ~ abelid0 with the telescoping ( ~ abelpd ) and the reindexing ( ~ abelrx ) carried out.

